      "side": 0,
      "message": "Yes, we\u0027ve \"hard-coded\" addresses from https://crosvm.dev/book/appendix/memory_layout.html in `vmbase::layout::crosvm` so yes, the previous code used to map the entirety of \"low-address\" MMIO (`0x0` to `0x4000_0000`, IIRC, which was recently bumped to `0x7fc0_0000`).\n\nFor the attributes, see `libs/libvmbase/src/memory/page_table.rs`:\n```\nconst DEVICE_NGNRE: Attributes \u003d Attributes::ATTRIBUTE_INDEX_0;\nconst DEVICE_LAZY: Attributes \u003d\n    MMIO_LAZY_MAP_FLAG.union(DEVICE_NGNRE).union(Attributes::UXN).union(Attributes::ACCESSED);\nconst DEVICE: Attributes \u003d DEVICE_LAZY.union(Attributes::VALID);\n```\nwhere `ATTRIBUTE_INDEX_0` indexes the MAIR, from `libs/libvmbase/entry.S`:\n```\n.set .L_MAIR_DEV_nGnRE,\t0x04\n.set .L_MAIR_MEM_WBWA,\t0xff\n.set .Lmairval, .L_MAIR_DEV_nGnRE | (.L_MAIR_MEM_WBWA \u003c\u003c 8)\n\nmov_i x30, .Lmairval\nmsr mair_el1, x30\n```",
